# Vendor APT repositories, written by script/apt-vendor (ADR-003).
# One repository per line, nine whitespace-separated columns:
#   id        repository id; the file is /etc/apt/sources.list.d/<id>.sources
#   profile   the profile that selects it (script/lib/profiles.sh validates the name)
#   target    both | linux | wsl: where it may be written
#   uri       the repository URI, without a trailing slash
#   suite     a literal suite, or @codename for the machine's VERSION_CODENAME;
#             "/" marks a flat repository
#   comps     the components, comma separated; "-" for none (flat repositories)
#   key       keyring id; apt/keys/<key>.asc is installed as /etc/apt/keyrings/<key>.asc.
#             One keyring per vendor: repositories of one vendor share it
#   fpr       the full 40-hex fingerprint of the key's primary key; the install is
#             refused before any write when apt/keys/<key>.asc does not match
#   packages  the packages this repository supplies, comma separated; unpinned (ADR-011)
# Suites were checked against the vendors' Release indexes on 2026-11-26: docker and
# azure-cli publish "resolute" (Ubuntu 26.04); the other three are release-agnostic.
# The NVIDIA repository is architecture-specific; this repository is x86_64 only.
